fest.py`)\\nRather than scanning individual 0x addresses in isolation, each target is cataloged as a system:\\n```python\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass ProtocolComponent:\\n    address: str\\n    role: str  # USER_ENTRYPOINT, VAULT, LENDING_POOL, ORACLE, TIMELOCK, TOKEN\\n    proxy_type: Optional[str] = None\\n    implementation_address: Optional[str] = None\\n    source_dir: Optional[str] = None\\n    abi: List[Dict] = field(default_factory=list)\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass ProtocolScopeManifest:\\n    protocol_id: str\\n    chain_id: int\\n    pinned_block\\n\u003ctruncated 3893 bytes\u003e\\nnce-First Verdict Profiles (Replacing Confidence Score)\\nReplace the single percentage score with an explicit 6-dimension evidence record:\\n\\n| Dimension | Assessment Basis |\\n| :--- | :--- |\\n| **Reachability** | Proven callable from unprivileged actor through active entrypoint |\\n| **State Feasibility** | Preconditions exist on live pinned snapshot or are reachable via valid actions |\\n| **Property Validity** | Violates an approved invariant (not intended administrative power) |\\n| **Impact Demonstrated** | Quantified financial loss, insolvency, or unauthorized takeover |\\n| **Reproduction** | Deterministic Foundry test passes locally and triggers counterexample |\\n| **Scope** | Confirmed on proxy system (not isolated implementation shell) |\\n\\n**Status Labels:**\\n`STATIC_CANDIDATE` $\\\\rightarrow$ `PROPERTY_APPROVED` $\\\\rightarrow$ `FORK_SIMULATED` $\\\\rightarrow$ `COUNTEREXAMPLE_FOUND` $\\\\rightarrow$ `CONFIRMED_EXPLOIT`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Phased Implementation Plan\\n\\n```\\nPhase 1: Vault System Adapter End-to-End (Starting Implementation)\\n ├── 1.1 Manifest \u0026 Dependency parser for ERC-4626 Vaults (e.g. Euler / Yearn / Morpho Vaults)\\n ├── 1.2 Property catalog: Value conservation, first-depositor dilution, share price inflation\\n ├── 1.3 Multi-actor Foundry invariant handler generator (ghost accounting, deal fixtures)\\n └── 1.4 Pinned RPC fork runner + Counterexample trace visualizer\\n\\nPhase 2: Economic Search \u0026 Dependency Fixtures\\n ├── 2.1 Foundry optimization invariant mode (maximizing net gain)\\n ├── 2.2 Token quirk fixtures (Fee-on-transfer, missing returns, re-entrancy callbacks)\\n └── 2.3 Halmos integration for bounded rounding and conversion math verification\\n\\nPhase 3: Benchmark Corpus \u0026 Scaling\\n ├── 3.1 Versioned regression benchmark (Known exploits + Patched PR counterparts)\\n └── 3.2 Automated protocol expansion across Lending, Staking, and Messaging\\n```\\n\\nWe can begin Phase 1 immediately by setting up the ERC-4626 Vault system adapter and multi-actor Foundry invariant handler template.\",\"thinking\":\"Recognized the user's architectural specification as a clear roadmap. The suggested workflow appears robust: it moves from defining the protocol and constraints to generating tests and refining counterexamples. The presence of initial invariant generation in the code base is a positive signal.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}"}
{"File":"/Users/markstevenson/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/c811d9fe-ab1c-4316-96e0-4960828be7a2/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl","LineNumber":1666,"LineContent":"{\"step_index\":1675,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-11T16:17:24Z\",\"content\":\"**Phase 3** has been completed, tested, committed, and pushed to GitHub:\\n\\n**Commit:** [`63736fc`](https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline/commit/63736fc)  \\n**Branch:** `main` at [https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline](https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Deliverables Implemented in Phase 3\\n\\n#### 1. Versioned Regression Benchmark Corpus ([`core/benchmark_corpus.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/benchmark_corpus.py))\\nCreated a standardized regression benchmark suite matching vulnerable implementations against their patched counterparts to prevent regressions and eliminate vacuous test campaigns:\\n- **`BENCH_01_VAULT_INFLATION` (ERC-4626 Share Dilution):**\\n  - *Vulnerable:* Standard unbacked initial ratio leading to 0-share victim dilution (`(assets * totalSupply) / totalAssets`).\\n  - *Patched:* OpenZeppelin-style virtual shares and decimal offset (`VIRTUAL_OFFSET = 1e3`), guaranteeing non-zero shares and bounded dilution.\\n- **`BENCH_02_INITIALIZER_TAKEOVER` (Uninitialized Implementation):**\\n  - *Vulnerable:* Logic contract deployable without initializing the implementation storage shell.\\n  - *Patched:* Constructor invoking `_disableInitializers()` / initialization lock on creation.\\n- **`BENCH_03_FEE_ON_TRANSFER_ACCOUNTING` (Balance Desynchronization):**\\n  - *Vulnerable:* Crediting user balance based on nominal input argument.\\n  - *Patched:* Measuring authentic received balance delta (`balanceAfter - balanceBefore`).\\n\\nEmitted test contracts and harnesses into [`tests/exploit_validation/benchmark/`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/tests/exploit_validation/benchmark/).\\n\\n#### 2. Benchmark Precision \u0026 Specificity Evaluator ([`BenchmarkRunner`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/benchmark_corpus.py#L274-L342))\\n- Evaluates test harnesses against both vulnerable contracts and patched counterparts.\\n- Asserts that:\\n  1. Counterexamples trigger on the defect (True Positive rate = 100%).\\n\u003ctruncated 201 bytes\u003e\\ners/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/tests/test_phase3_benchmark_and_scaling.py).\\n- All 24 tests across all three phases pass cleanly (`pytest tests/`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Complete v2 Architecture Overview\\n\\n| Phase | Core Deliverables | Location / Commits |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Phase 1: Vault System Adapter** | Protocol Scope Manifest, Property Catalog, Multi-Actor Invariant Fuzzing Harness, 6-Dimension Evidence Profiler | [`core/protocol_manifest.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/protocol_manifest.py), [`core/property_catalog.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/property_catalog.py), [`core/vault_harness_generator.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/vault_harness_generator.py), [`core/fork_runner.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/fork_runner.py) ([`054c7be`](https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline/commit/054c7be)) |\\n| **Phase 2: Economic Search \u0026 Fixtures** | Marked-to-Market Optimization Fuzzer, Hazardous Token \u0026 Oracle Fixtures, Selective Halmos Symbolic Verifier | [`core/economic_optimizer.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/economic_optimizer.py), [`core/dependency_fixtures.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/dependency_fixtures.py), [`core/symbolic_verifier.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/symbolic_verifier.py) ([`ade1c8a`](https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline/commit/ade1c8a)) |\\n| **Phase 3: Benchmark Corpus \u0026 Scaling** | Versioned Regression Benchmark Suite, Vulnerable vs Patched Baselines, Precision/Recall Metrics Engine | [`core/benchmark_corpus.py`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/core/benchmark_corpus.py), [`tests/exploit_validation/benchmark/`](file:///Users/markstevenson/Documents/eth-audit-pipeline/tests/exploit_validation/benchmark/) ([`63736fc`](https://github.com/markstevenson15/eth-audit-pipeline/commit/63736fc)) |\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}"}
